{"recall":{"defs":[["Logistic regression","Linear model + sigmoid for binary classification."],["Logit","Pre-activation z = wᵀx."],["Decision boundary","wᵀx = 0, a hyperplane."],["Binary cross-entropy","−[y log ŷ + (1 − y) log(1 − ŷ)]."],["SGD","Update from one random example."],["One-hot","Length-K vector with a single 1."],["Softmax","e^{z_k}/Σ e^{z_j}."],["Mini-batch","B examples per update; ⌈N/B⌉ per epoch."],["Macro vs weighted average","Equal weight per class vs by class frequency."]],"formulas":["\\hat y=\\sigma(\\mathbf w^T\\mathbf x)=\\frac1{1+e^{-\\mathbf w^T\\mathbf x}}","\\sigma'(z)=\\sigma(z)(1-\\sigma(z))","J=-\\frac1N\\sum[y\\log\\hat y+(1-y)\\log(1-\\hat y)]","\\nabla\\ell=(\\hat y-y)\\mathbf x","\\hat y_k=\\frac{e^{z_k}}{\\sum_je^{z_j}},\\ Z=XW","J(W)=-\\frac1N\\sum_i\\sum_ky_k\\log\\hat y_k","\\nabla J_{\\mathcal B}=\\frac1BX_{\\mathcal B}^T(\\hat Y_{\\mathcal B}-Y_{\\mathcal B})","P=\\frac{TP}{TP+FP},\\ R=\\frac{TP}{TP+FN},\\ F1=\\frac{2PR}{P+R}"],"takeaways":["Sigmoid for binary, softmax for multi-class.","Cross-entropy loss; gradient = (prediction − label) × input.","SGD / mini-batch SGD instead of full-batch GD.","Accuracy misleads on imbalanced data; use precision/recall/F1.","Stable softmax: subtract the max logit."],"confused":[["Precision vs recall","Correct among predicted positives vs found among actual positives."],["Iteration vs epoch","One update vs one pass over the data."],["Multi-class vs multi-label","Softmax (exactly one) vs independent sigmoids (any subset)."],["Macro vs weighted","Each class equal vs by support."],["Logits vs probabilities","Unbounded scores vs softmax outputs."]],"minute":"Binary classification uses logistic regression: z = wᵀx, ŷ = σ(z) = P(y = 1 | x), predict 1 when z ≥ 0, so the boundary is the hyperplane wᵀx = 0. Training minimises binary cross-entropy, the Bernoulli negative log-likelihood, whose gradient is (ŷ − y)x; SGD applies it one shuffled example at a time (the two steps take w from (0, 0) to (−0.25, −0.25) to (0.116, 0.847)). Evaluate with the confusion matrix, accuracy, precision, recall and F1. Multi-class uses one-hot labels, a (d + 1) × K weight matrix, logits Z = XW and softmax, with categorical cross-entropy and mini-batch gradient Xᵀ(Ŷ − Y)/B; ⌈N/B⌉ updates per epoch, B usually 128–256. Predict with argmax of softmax, and report per-class metrics with macro or weighted averaging and top-k accuracy. Use stable softmax (subtract the max), standardised features and shuffling."},"flashcards":[["Classification types","Binary, multi-class (exactly one of K), multi-label (any subset)"],["Why not linear regression for classification","Outputs can be < 0 or > 1; need [0, 1]"],["Logistic regression (1)","$\\hat y=\\sigma(\\mathbf w^T\\mathbf x)$"],["Sigmoid derivative","$\\sigma'(z)=\\sigma(z)(1-\\sigma(z))$; max 0.25 at 0"],["Decision boundary","$\\mathbf w^T\\mathbf x=0$ (ŷ = 0.5)"],["Binary cross-entropy (7)","$-[y\\log\\hat y+(1-y)\\log(1-\\hat y)]$"],["SGD gradient (10)","$(\\hat y-y)\\mathbf x$"],["Study-hours example after 2 SGD steps","w = (0.116, 0.847)"],["Precision / recall","TP/(TP+FP) / TP/(TP+FN)"],["F1","Harmonic mean $2PR/(P+R)$"],["Weight matrix shape (multi-class)","$(d+1)\\times K$"],["Softmax (17)","$e^{z_k}/\\sum_je^{z_j}$"],["Softmax(2, 1, 0.1)","(0.659, 0.242, 0.099)"],["Categorical cross-entropy (22)","$-\\frac1N\\sum_i\\sum_ky_k\\log\\hat y_k$"],["Iterations per epoch (23)","$\\lceil N/B\\rceil$; 469 for 60,000 / 128"],["Mini-batch gradient (25)","$\\frac1BX_{\\mathcal B}^T(\\hat Y_{\\mathcal B}-Y_{\\mathcal B})$"],["Inference example","z = (1.2, 2.5, 0.8) → class 2 at 68.7%"],["Macro vs weighted (35–36)","$\\frac1K\\sum_k$ vs $\\sum_k\\frac{N_k}{N}$"],["Top-k accuracy (37)","True class among k highest probabilities"],["Stable softmax","Subtract $c=\\max_kz_k$ before exponentiating"]],"coverage":{"topics":[{"simple":["what","h1"],"deep":["n4-class","n4-classex","n4-types"],"viz":[],"status":"complete"},{"simple":["why","h1"],"deep":["n4-